window.docContents[234].resolve({"/Judgments-and-domains/Static-judgments/#Core-C_________-natural-semantics--Judgments-and-domains--Static-judgments":{"contents":"The judgment  states that the expression  has type  in the context . One rule per constructor of Expr.\n\nThe judgment  holds for the expressions that denote a location. In the current subset, only the variable.\n\nThe judgment  states that the command  is well typed and extends  to , so that a declaration reaches the following commands of the sequence. The return type  of the enclosing function is an implicit parameter.\n\n","context":"Core C++, natural semantics\u0009Judgments and domains","header":"1.2. Static judgments","id":"/Judgments-and-domains/Static-judgments/#Core-C_________-natural-semantics--Judgments-and-domains--Static-judgments"}});